  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>As we know, if the line <math><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></math> is a tangent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mi>y</mi></math>, then <math><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mrow><mi>m</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>.</p><p>So, equation of tangent with slope <math><mi>m</mi></math> is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>i</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>Since, tangent is inclined at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi></math> with the positive <math><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo></math> axis, i.e.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>tan</mi><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></math>.</p><p>Equation of tangent is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>tan</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#8289;</mo><mi>&#952;</mi></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">cot</mi></mrow><mo>&#8289;</mo><mrow><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></mrow></mrow></math></p><p><math><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext>&#8201;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math></p>"
